1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,810
Measuring angles with length?
Radians

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:06,230
We usually measure angles in degrees (°)
One full turn = 360°

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,400
This time, cut a string as long as the radius

4
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:11,670
and wrap it around the circle

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,540
The angle one string makes = 1 radian
(about 57.3°)

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:18,710
So how many strings fit
in half a turn?

7
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:22,580
3 and a bit more… 3.14… strings = π!

8
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:26,450
Half a turn = π, a full turn = 2π
We count angles in "how many radii"

9
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,950
So with radians,
arc length is just one multiplication!

10
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:34,700
NEXT: Is the sine graph
a circle's shadow?
